# Airseekers Tron mower — ROS 2 port handoff bundle

Collected on the robot itself on 2026-10-05 (serial no. in `/meta/sn` on the device, firmware
`v1.3.27-rc.1-tron+20260713`). Everything here was gathered **read-only**; nothing on the mower
was changed. Target: a ROS 2 driver stack modelled on OpenMower / MowgliNext that talks to the
Airseekers mainboard MCUs directly.

Start with `00_docs/` (the earlier full system survey), then `01_mcu_protocol/`.

## TL;DR for the agent doing the port

1. **The MCU serial protocol is fully recoverable.** `01_mcu_protocol/protocol_definitions_recovered.h`
   is the stripped vendor header regenerated from DWARF debug info left in `libmower_sdk.a`
   (struct layouts, offsets, both enums). `mcu_frame_decode.py` decodes/encodes frames and was
   validated on 172,850 live frames with zero checksum errors. Byte order is little-endian.
2. **Wire format:** `A5 | total_len | {sub_len type mod payload}+ | sum&0xFF | 5A`, with
   `F5 01/02/03` byte-stuffing for `A5/5A/F5`. Host→MCU `type=0`, MCU→host `type=8`,
   heartbeat `type=255`. Module ids: speed 4, battery 5, imu 9, sensor 10, cutter 11, version 12,
   motors 13, calib 18, log 19, bms_version 24, charge 3.
3. **Port:** `/dev/serial_mower` → `ttyS9` (RK3588 UART9 @ `0xfebc0000`), 115200 8N1. The cutter
   board is the gateway; the chassis board hangs off it over a second UART. IMU is a separate
   **WIT-Motion JY61P** on `/dev/serial_imu` (`ttyS1`, 115200, standard WIT 0x55 frames — public
   protocol). GNSS is a **Unicore UM960** on `/dev/serial_rtk` (`ttyS4`). BLE module on
   `/dev/serial_ble` (`ttyS3`).
4. **Firmware for every MCU** is in `02_mcu_firmware/` together with the OTA flasher (`ota.py`)
   which also documents the bootloader protocol. Do not flash anything until the driver works.
5. **Unknowns to resolve on hardware** (marked `(?)` in the header): heartbeat period and
   failsafe behaviour, units of `BatteryInfo.current` / `MotorInfo.*`, meaning of module id 7,
   the exact semantics of `SensorInfoControl`, and whether `SendImuData` is required by the MCU.

## What is in here

| Dir | Contents |
|---|---|
| `00_docs/` | The 10-document system survey from 2026-10-02 (hardware, closed-source inventory, BLE, HTTP/MQTT APIs, reuse strategy, cautions) plus vendor `.proto`, `.srv`, OpenAPI. |
| `01_mcu_protocol/` | **The core.** `protocol_definitions_recovered.h`, `mcu_frame_decode.py`, `sdk_static_lib/libmower_sdk.a` (+ extracted `.o` with full DWARF, `nm` symbol list), `dwarf/` (raw type dumps + the `dwarf2hdr.py` script that produced them), `bin/` (`mower_base_node`, and two **standalone non-ROS test tools** `mower_sdk_test` / `mower_sdk_ncurses` that drive the MCU directly), `libs/` (the 4 private `.so` the node links), `mower_base_pkg/` (package incl. Chinese design docs `docs/aichw_mower.md` describing the original **ROS 2 Humble** version of this driver, config, launch, URDFs, test scripts), `base_imu_pkg/`, `mcu_traffic_logs/` (raw MCU→host captures), `ota_tools/`, `mower_base_node_strings.txt` (topics/params/symbols from the stripped node). |
| `02_mcu_firmware/` | `mcu_bin_v1.3.27/`: chassis (`0.6.14`–`0.6.34`, latest **0.6.34**), cutter (`0.6.21`–`0.6.36`, latest **0.6.36**), battery/BMS (`1.14.0`–`1.18.0`, latest **1.18.0**), rtk_rover (`0.7.x/0.8.x/0.9.x` by board rev `-addr 0/1/2`, latest 0.7.32/0.8.32/0.9.50), rtk_rover_m4 LoRa (`B039.01.02.dwn`), rtk_station, `emmc/emmc.img` (DDR-frequency config blob flashed at eMMC sector 0x40, SN-gated), `ota.py`, `install.sh`, `install.py`, `rtk_rover_m4/mcu_m4_ota.py`. Plus older rtk_rover binaries only present in the v1.0.60 OTA. All are **Artery AT32** application images (raw `.bin`, 20–65 KB). The versions running right now: cutter 0.6.36, chassis 0.6.34, BMS 1.18.0, rtk 0.9.50. |
| `03_ros_interfaces/` | `mower_msgs` (88 msg/srv/action), `mower_gps_msgs`, `mower_proto` (19 `.proto`, BLE/MQTT payloads), `vanjee_lidar_msg`, and the generated headers that only exist in `devel/` (`mower_logic`, `mower_bt_nodes`, `mpc_controller`, …). |
| `04_full_src_tree/` | Complete `/workspace/src` (no `.git`, no `.rknn`) + `install.sh`, `profile/`, build version. 52 of 72 packages are binary-only but every `package.xml`, `CMakeLists.txt`, launch, param YAML and the ~900 surviving headers (controller, localisation, planner interfaces) are here. Also contains the vendor SDK libs: Metoak `libMoGeneralSDK` (`mower_drivers/base_stereo/sdk_v2745/lib`, `mower_perception/vslam_ros/3rdparty/metoak/lib`), `librknnrt.so` (`mower_perception/rknn2_runtime/librknn_api/aarch64`), Rockchip MPP (`base_cameras/lib/mpp`), `libws_2812.so` (`mower_task/mower_light_sound/lib`). |
| `05_driver_binaries/` | Hardware-abstraction nodes with no source: `base_ble_node`, `mower_gps_driver_node(+ntrip)`, `base_cameras_node`, `mower_light_sound_node`, `base_keys_node`, `base_net_node`, `mower_charge`, `stereo_ros`, `fake_rtk_node`, `fake_mower_node` (simulator), `gatt-service`; `libs/` with their private `.so`; `ldd_report.txt` lists what each needs outside the system. |
| `06_vendor_sdks/` | Metoak camera tools + kernel modules (`ko/`), the custom OpenCV 4.2 (`/usr/metoak/4.2.0-gcc930`) every closed binary links against, AP6256 BT/Wi-Fi firmware (`BCM4345C5.hcd`), `librga`. See its README. |
| `07_system_config/` | `udev/mower.rules` (the device-name mapping), all `mower-*.service` units, cron/logrotate/resolved/NetworkManager snippets, `mower_cam_keeper.py`, unit enablement state. |
| `08_calibration_identity/` | Stereo intrinsics/extrinsics (`cam0/cam1/stereo_params.yaml`, camera SN IC17SZ01011), the Metoak camera EEPROM calibration dump, `base_cameras` configs, URDFs (`m2-11`…`m2-16`, `urdf.py` picks by SN). |
| `09_platform/` | Device-tree blob (`device-tree.dtb`, decompile with `dtc -I dtb -O dts`), kernel cmdline, eMMC partition map, UART/I²C/sysfs mapping, `lsmod`, `dpkg -l`, ROS debs, live tty settings. |
| `10_ros_live_snapshot/` | `rosnode/rostopic/rosservice` listings, per-node pub/sub/service tables for the driver nodes, one sample message per MCU-side topic, measured rates. |
| `11_perception_models/` | The five `.rknn` NPU models (YOLOv8 det ×2, PP-LiteSeg ×2, light classifier). Not needed for the MCU work; included because they have no source. |

Full OTA images (incl. the 798 MB `devel/` tree) remain on the device at
`/userdata/RobotData/upgrade/*.tar.gz` if anything else is ever needed.

## Hardware ↔ Linux device map (verified live)

| Function | Device | Hardware | Owner process today | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Cutter+chassis MCU bus | `/dev/serial_mower` → `ttyS9` (UART9, `febc0000`) | Artery AT32 boards | `mower_base_node` | 115200 8N1, this protocol |
| IMU | `/dev/serial_imu` → `ttyS1` (UART1, `feb40000`) | WIT-Motion JY61P | `mower_base_node` (via `libbase_imu.so`) | configured by `wit_imu_config.py` (100 Hz, 98 Hz BW) |
| GNSS/RTK rover | `/dev/serial_rtk` → `ttyS4` (UART4, `feb70000`) | Unicore UM960 + AT32 rtk board + LoRa M4 | `mower_gps_driver_node` | NMEA + Unicore binary; `ota.py -t 21 -m 37` for the rtk board; `mcu_m4_ota.py` for LoRa |
| BLE link to app | `/dev/serial_ble` → `ttyS3` (UART3, `feb60000`) | external BLE UART module | `base_ble_node` | framing source in `base_ble/src`; alt. path via AP6256 on `ttyS5` + socat (disabled) |
| LTE | `/dev/serial_lte` → `ttyUSB2` | Quectel EC200A-EU | `lte.py` | |
| LEDs | `/dev/spidev3.0` | WS2812 strip | `mower_light_sound_node` (`libws_2812.so`) | |
